    description: |
    # How to Add a New SmartLayout Template

    ## 1. Component Structure
    SmartLayout templates are implemented in the following locations:

    ### Core Components
    - `src/elements/smartLayout/SmartLayout.tsx` - Main editor component
    - `src/elements/smartLayout/SmartLayoutView.tsx` - View component for presentations
    - `src/elements/smartLayout/components/` - Directory for template implementations

    ## 2. Creating New Template Components

    1. Create a new directory in `src/elements/smartLayout/components/` for your template:
    ```
    src/elements/smartLayout/components/YourTemplate/
    ├── YourTemplate.tsx         # Editor component
    ├── YourTemplateView.tsx     # View component
    └── types.ts                 # Template-specific types
    ```

    2. Implement the editor component (`YourTemplate.tsx`):
    ```typescript
    interface YourTemplateProps {
        elementId: string;
        presentationId: string;
        slideId: string;
        layoutId: string;
        tiptapRefs: RefObject<TipTapRefs>;
        isFocused: boolean;
    }

    const YourTemplate: React.FC<YourTemplateProps> = ({...props}) => {
        // Implementation
    };
    ```

    3. Implement the view component (`YourTemplateView.tsx`):
    ```typescript
    interface YourTemplateViewProps {
        element: SmartLayoutElement;
        presentationId: string;
        slideId: string;
        layoutId: string;
        tiptapRefs: RefObject<TipTapRefs> | null;
        isFocused: boolean;
    }

    const YourTemplateView: React.FC<YourTemplateViewProps> = ({...props}) => {
        // Implementation
    };
    ```

    ## 3. Registering the Template

    1. Add your template variant to the SmartLayout type in `src/types/elements.ts`:
    ```typescript
    type SmartLayoutVariant = 
        | 'images-with-text'
        | 'text-boxes'
        | 'your-template-variant';
    ```

    2. Add the template to SmartLayout switch statement in both files:
    - `src/elements/smartLayout/SmartLayout.tsx`:
    ```typescript
    case 'your-template-variant':
        return (
            <YourTemplate
                elementId={elementId}
                tiptapRefs={tiptapRefs}
                presentationId={presentationId}
                slideId={slideId}
                layoutId={layoutId}
                isFocused={isFocused}
            />
        );
    ```

    - `src/elements/smartLayout/SmartLayoutView.tsx`:
    ```typescript
    case 'your-template-variant':
        return (
            <YourTemplateView
                element={element}
                tiptapRefs={tiptapRefs}
                presentationId={presentationId}
                slideId={slideId}
                layoutId={layoutId}
                isFocused={isFocused}
            />
        );
    ```

    ## 4. Adding Template to Slash Menu

    1. Update the slash menu commands in `src/components/editor/SlideMenu/SlashCommands/commands.ts`:
    ```typescript
    {
        title: 'Your Template',
        description: 'Description of your template',
        icon: YourTemplateIcon,
        command: ({ editor }) => {
            // Implementation
        }
    }
    ```

    ## 5. Adding Template to Right Panel

    1. Update the SmartLayout settings component in `src/elements/smartLayout/components/SmartLayoutSettings/SmartLayoutSettings.tsx`:
    ```typescript
    const templateOptions = [
        { value: 'your-template-variant', label: 'Your Template' },
        // ... other options
    ];
    ```

    ## 6. Template Preview/Live View Integration

    The template will automatically work in preview/live view once you've:
    1. Implemented the view component (`YourTemplateView.tsx`)
    2. Registered it in `SmartLayoutView.tsx`
    3. Properly handled all required props and state management

    ## Best Practices

    1. Follow existing template patterns (like `ImagesWithText` or `TextBoxes`)
    2. Implement proper TypeScript types for your template
    3. Handle all required props and state management
    4. Implement proper error handling
    5. Follow the project's styling conventions (using TailwindCSS)
    6. Add accessibility attributes to interactive elements

    ## Testing

    1. Test the template in editor mode
    2. Test the template in view mode
    3. Test the template in different screen sizes
    4. Test all interactive features
    5. Test error states and edge cases
